codex
The proof audit gives a more precise outcome: the finite bound is uniform in the spike count if a stated radial-moment bound holds. Without that hypothesis, P40 forces either an unbalanced-relation defect or a large balanced moment. Pairwise separation does not control the latter; the report includes an exactly graded family whose fourth moment grows with the number of spikes.

I also proved a stable version of the Gram defect bound, independent of dimension. It gives the needed residual estimate if a finite binary reconstruction has small total negative spectral mass. Constructing that reconstruction uniformly in the window count remains the missing step.
