I strengthened the radial obstruction with an actual binary construction at density 1/2. Its frequencies are pairwise separated and its normalized individual amplitudes tend to zero, yet the normalized fourth moment grows linearly with the number of frequencies.

It captures only a small fraction of the variance, so it leaves TL1 intact. It does show that any uniform radial-moment argument must use an additional hypothesis, such as near-exhaustion of the binary spectrum.
