Completed the research brief and saved the full [tdense5 report](/Users/jmercedes/Desktop/Projects/Research/chowla-cosine/.research/agents/tdense5_report.md).

The report contains:

- **PROVED on paper:** finite TL1 with explicit polynomial, relation-count, centering, and large-sieve errors; a version uniform in the spike count under a stated radial-moment hypothesis; and the sharp Gaussian constant 2/π.
- **PROVED reductions:** an exact cyclic connection to P40, sliding-block energy identities, and a dimension-independent stable Gram defect bound.
- **PROVED obstruction:** actual binary words at density 1/2 showing that pair separation and small individual amplitudes do not imply uniform radial-moment control.
- **NUMERICAL validation:** 90 saved sets, 360 tall-spectrum diagnostics, 360 cyclic checks, and passing exact integer/rational checks. All calculations ran on `34.148.157.169` through `src/dirun.sh -c 2`.

**T-dense and J-uniform QD remain unproved.** The report identifies the precise uniformity losses and states one sufficient missing lemma—height-uniform binary spectral completion—whose proof would close the capture argument.

The [reproduction script](/Users/jmercedes/Desktop/Projects/Research/chowla-cosine/.research/agents/tdense5_scratch/audit.py), [results summary](/Users/jmercedes/Desktop/Projects/Research/chowla-cosine/.research/agents/tdense5_scratch/summary.json), and [artifact manifest](/Users/jmercedes/Desktop/Projects/Research/chowla-cosine/.research/agents/tdense5_scratch/manifest.json) are saved. No commits or subagents were used.
